---
/* The map's story, told in Plum's editorial voice. It appears twice — on the
 * intro, where it is the first thing a visitor reads, and in the About panel
 * behind the P-heart — so it lives here rather than being written out twice
 * and drifting apart. Styles hang off .about-copy in prompt-map.css.
 *
 * The heading level is a prop because of that reuse: the page would otherwise
 * carry two <h1>s saying the same thing. The intro takes the h1 — it is the
 * page's only one, and the first thing read — while the About panel takes an h3
 * beneath the "About" h2 it already sits under.
 */
import { SUGGEST_FORM } from '../lib/intents.js';
import Credits from './Credits.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
const { headingLevel = 'h3' } = Astro.props;
const Heading = headingLevel;
---

<Heading class="lead">Why we made this</Heading>
<p>Health is having a moment. It has been, for a while. And yet, for a lot of us, the moment we decide to actually do something about it, we pause. Where do you start? What's near you? Is that place your colleague keeps posting about actually any good, or is it just well-lit?</p>
<p>At Plum, we've always thought of health as a lifestyle thing as much as a preventive and emergency thing – the walk you take, the class you show up to, the people you end up seeing every Tuesday because you both keep turning up. Making health more accessible starts, we think, with making you aware of what's already around you. The places. The events. The small, ordinary communities you could choose to become part of.</p>
<p>It's also why we've partnered with some of the loveliest health and wellness brands in the country, so there's a good discount waiting for you when you get there. Those spots are marked on the map, with a link to the Plum app.</p>
<p>This is by no means an exhaustive list. So if you know something we’ve missed, write to us. Or <a class="about-form-link" href={SUGGEST_FORM} target="_blank" rel="noopener">fill this form</a>.</p>
<p>Prefer to read rather than pan? <a class="about-form-link" href={`${base}list`}>Every place on the map, as a list</a>.</p>
<p>This map is heavily inspired by <a class="about-form-link" href="https://www.bangalorestartupmap.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">bangalorestartupmap.com</a>. Thank you, Aditi Tibarewal for thinking it up.</p>
<Credits class="about-credits" />
